do Infer the intention from the sentence after /inux estimate or the equivalent
    plain-language estimate request. Return an object
    with unchanged request and mode: "create" for an empty template (the default
    without a sentence), "improve" for requested edits, "generate" for a complete
    estimate, or "publish" for explicit Jira publication. Use null for unsupported,
    conflicting, or ambiguous requests. Do not inspect the project or tools. as @route

set request = @route.request
set mode = @route.mode

if @mode == "create"
    use estimate-create.flow
    return

if @mode == "improve"
    use estimate-improve.flow
    return

if @mode == "generate"
    use estimate-generate.flow
    return

if @mode == "publish"
    use estimate-publish.flow
    return

return "Usage: /inux estimate [request]. Create an empty template, improve it, generate a complete estimate, or publish to Jira."
